id: pmc-rdc3
title: Repository-local pm 2026.8.6 prepare removes the 2026.8.7 extension merge fence
description: "The package is released as 2026.8.7 but its dev dependency and lock resolve @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.6. A real npm ci runs scripts/prepare-merge-driver.mjs through that stale local CLI and deletes the required extensions no-merge and managed-manifest pm-json rules from .gitattributes. Align the runtime tooling with installed pm 2026.8.7, replace the JavaScript lifecycle with erasable TypeScript, make target-platform command resolution safe, and cover the lifecycle as authored source."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[6]: bug,merge-safety,multi-agent,pm-cli-2026.8.7,release-blocker,typescript
created_at: "2026-08-07T20:46:00.720Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T21:28:02.026Z"
deadline: "2026-08-08T20:46:00.720Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T21:13:02.559Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T21:13:02.559Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: npm ci with the package-local pm 2026.8.7 preserves the canonical .agents/pm/extensions/** -merge and .managed-extensions.json merge=pm-json rules; the lifecycle is erasable TypeScript with no dynamic or inline imports and propagates real installation failures; target-platform POSIX and Windows PATH/PATHEXT behavior is covered; all lifecycle source has exact 100/100/100 coverage and is included in the fail-closed measured set; npm and Bun release gates and fresh installed-pm acceptance pass; no publication occurs without history privacy clearance and maintainer approval
definition_of_ready: "Reproduce the deletion with npm ci, compare package-local pm 2026.8.6 with host-installed pm 2026.8.7, and confirm no existing active item tracks this exact regression"
value: Concurrent agents retain the generated-extension merge boundary after dependency installation
impact: Prevents npm ci from silently weakening PM merge safety and reintroducing invalid extension artifact merges
outcome: pm-changelog uses current pm 2026.8.7 lifecycle behavior without authored JavaScript and fails closed across supported platforms
why_now: The required baseline coverage run reproduced tracked merge-fence deletion in the canonical package
reviewer: maintainer
risk: critical
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-compatibility
release: Unreleased
reporter: codex
severity: critical
environment: Clean pm-changelog worktree at v2026.8.7 using npm ci
repro_steps: "Run npm ci, then inspect the pm-cli managed block in .gitattributes; package-local @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.6 removes the two extension rules while host pm 2026.8.7 includes them in dry-run output"
resolution: "Updated and locked pm CLI 2026.8.7, replaced the JavaScript prepare hook with tested erasable TypeScript, added safe POSIX and Windows resolution, and enforced lifecycle coverage."
expected_result: npm ci retains both extension merge rules and lifecycle failures cannot be silently ignored.
actual_result: The gitattributes hash is identical before and after npm ci; local pm is 2026.8.7; 12 lifecycle tests and all package gates and fresh acceptance checks pass.
affected_version: 2026.8.7
fixed_version: Unreleased
component: fleet/merge-safety
regression: true
customer_impact: Multi-agent branches can merge generated extension assets incorrectly after a normal dependency install.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pmc-p5l1,related_to,"2026-08-07T20:46:00.720Z","harness:codex",coverage-discovery,asserted
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T20:46:00.720Z","harness:codex",Reproduced against the real package prepare lifecycle before source edits; this is separate from the cli.ts and extension.ts coverage deficit.
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T20:46:00.720Z","harness:codex",Package-local pm reports 2026.8.6 while host pm reports 2026.8.7. Only the host dry-run emits both canonical extension rules.
  "2026-08-07T21:12:49.725Z","harness:codex","Regression proof complete: npm ci resolved package-local @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7 and preserved .gitattributes byte-for-byte (SHA-256 ddc3bafc07ad7eafa9c67152e0c3ee2f8b81c52a9485ddee9277c7c0d7fcdccb before and after), including .agents/pm/extensions/** -merge and the managed manifest pm-json rule. Twelve lifecycle tests are exact 100/100/100; npm release check, Bun tarball CLI smoke, fresh pm install, package doctor, governed item creation, and changelog generation all pass."
  "2026-08-07T21:28:02.026Z","harness:codex",CodeRabbit correctly requested an asymmetric symlink fixture for the prepare entry guard. The guard now also catches missing argv paths before realpath comparison; the symlink and missing-path cases pass while lifecycle source remains exact 100/100/100.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T20:46:00.720Z","harness:codex",A package release version does not prove its development pm dependency is current; npm ci can silently rewrite tracked merge policy through prepare.
